the charges are upheld, Fennetcam Bannerwarg is gone. If the charges
aren't, then Bokum is gone. The raiser of charges thus faces risk as well.

I think it was the world football league (come on, sportsfans, what was
it?) that had something like this for instant replays. A coach could throw
a flag (red?) to have a play reviewed by replay. If the replay officials
overturned the field call, all the better for the coach. If the field call
was upheld, the coach's team lost a time-out. I'm fuzzy on the details
because I didn't watch these games, just remember seeing some headlines
about them a while back.

ho hO HO, Extropians. Marry Xmas.  What festivity trees will we decorate
