were not, they probably would not be realistic _transition_ plans:

finish my PhD; fulfill my current obligations (debts, family, friends,
government contracts, professional societies) and don't take on any
more; move to Hong Kong before it closes (visit Macau and Taiwan a lot);
move to Singapore when Hong Kong gets too dangerous even for me;
establish business offices in Japan, Singapore and New Zealand;
work hard on the technology with which individuals can enhance their
lives and especially their liberties; develop my own body and mind
(through a wide variety of techniques); ENJOY IT NOW (rather than
saying to myself, "I'll be really happy when <insert condition>.").

Mostly, I just ACT AS IF the world was what I wish it were, to the
extent that I can get away with it, and work to make it so.
I dunno if this is the kind of discussion you were trying to provoke,
Betsy... but it's where I am.  thanks.
